# =============================================================================
# Store — CREATE requests (VS Code REST Client) — POST /api/v1/stores (ADMIN)
# =============================================================================
# Semantics: creates a store, self-contained — one NON-CLOSED store per
# store admin (ticket 0010, Q5). Closing a store releases its admin's seat,
# so a manager whose only store was closed can take a new one (proven in
# requests 9–11); a manager whose store is still open cannot double-hold
# (request 9).
#   - Operating hours are optional at create (ticket 0011): openTime,
#     closeTime, workingDays (day names). closeTime must be after openTime
#     when both arrive together (400 otherwise). Hours cases: requests 20–23.
#
# How to run:
#   1. Start the backend: `docker compose up -d --build` — http://localhost:4000
#   2. Click the "Send Request" CodeLens above any request, IN ORDER, in one
#      sitting (captures are session-scoped).
#
# Prerequisites (admin persona):
#   Signup admin@devtunde.com with Password123! once, then promote in MySQL:
#     update users set role = 'ROLE_ADMIN' where email = 'admin@devtunde.com';
#
# Notes:
#   - All data is FAKE (devtunde.com emails, Nigerian numbers).
#   - The automated suite for these endpoints: StoreApiTests (src/test/java).
#   - Re-runnable: the manager persona, brands and contact emails are minted
#     fresh each run with {{$timestamp}} — no 409 collisions with prior runs.
#     Duplicate-brand/email probes (7–8) CHAIN values from request 4's live
#     response instead of recomputing {{$timestamp}} (it re-evaluates per
#     send — chaining captures is the only reliable way to refer to a
#     minted value later).
#   - Access tokens expire after 15 MINUTES. If tokened requests suddenly 401,
#     re-send the SETUP requests from the top (they mint and re-capture).
#   - REST Client captures die on file/VS Code reopen. If you see raw {{...}}
#     template text being sent or sudden 500s, re-send the setup requests
#     from the top — never continue on a dead capture.
#   - Expected codes: 201 created, 400 invalid payload/ghost admin/bad
#     storeType/close-before-open hours, 401 no/invalid token, 403 non-admin,
#     409 duplicate brand, duplicate contact email, or admin already holds a
#     store, 204 close.
# =============================================================================

@storeUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/stores
@authUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth

### 1 — Setup: login the admin persona
# Expected: 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2 — Setup: signup the store manager (minted fresh each run)
# Expected: 201
# @name sellerSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Manager",
  "email": "probe-store-mgr-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234589"
}

### 3 — Setup: login the manager
# Expected: 200
# @name sellerLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{sellerSignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 4 — Create a store for the manager
# Expected: 201 — publicId, status ACTIVE, phone normalized to +2348012345678
# @name createOk
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Probe Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "description": "The chain's main store",
  "storeType": "FLAGSHIP",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "1 Admiralty Way, Lekki",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "probe-main-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 5 — No Authorization header
# Expected: 401
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "brand": "No Token Branch",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Somewhere",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "no-token-branch@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 6 — Garbage token
# Expected: 401
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-jwt

{
  "brand": "Garbage Token Branch",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Somewhere",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "garbage-token-branch@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 7 — Duplicate brand (chained from request 4's live response)
# Expected: 409 — "A store with this brand already exists."
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "{{createOk.response.body.brand}}",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Different address",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "dup-brand-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 8 — Duplicate contact email (chained from request 4's live response)
# Expected: 409 — uniqueness is per-field, isolated (brand is different here)
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Dup Email Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Somewhere else",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "{{createOk.response.body.contact.email}}"
  }
}

### 9 — Second store for the SAME admin (his first is still OPEN)
# Expected: 409 — "A store with this store admin already exists." One
# NON-CLOSED store per admin; the seat is occupied by request 4's store
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Seat Taker {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Somewhere",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "seat-taker-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 10 — Close request 4's store (releases the seat)
# Expected: 204
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{createOk.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 11 — Same admin takes a NEW store — the seat was released by the close
# Expected: 201 — Q5 proven end to end: close releases, reassignment works
# @name seatReleased
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Seat-Free Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "45 New Address, Ikeja",
    "phone": "08087654321",
    "email": "seat-free-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 12 — Ghost admin: storeAdminPublicId that does not resolve
# Expected: 400 — "Store admin not found" (payload problem, NOT a 404)
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Ghost Admin Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "KIOSK",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Nowhere Street",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "ghost-admin-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 13 — Blank brand
# Expected: 400 — "Brand is required"
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Somewhere",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "blank-brand-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 14 — Unknown storeType (not a legal enum value)
# Expected: 400, never 500 — the enum rejects it at deserialization
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Mall of Nonsense {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "MALL",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Nowhere Street",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "bad-type-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 15 — Garbage phone
# Expected: 400 — @ValidPhoneNumber rejects it before the service runs
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Bad Phone Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Somewhere",
    "phone": "not-a-phone",
    "email": "bad-phone-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 16 — Missing contact object entirely
# Expected: 400 — "Contact details are required"
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "No Contact Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}"
}

### 17 — Setup: signup the regular persona (fixed — she never holds a seat)
# Expected: 201 (409 if she already exists — either way the account exists)
# @name regularSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Bola Storeless",
  "email": "bola.storeless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234571"
}

### 18 — Setup: login the regular persona
# Expected: 200
# @name regularLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bola.storeless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 19 — Create as a regular user
# Expected: 403 — store creation is admin-only (@PreAuthorize)
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{regularLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Nope Store",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{regularLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Somewhere",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "nope-store@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 20 — Setup: signup a second manager for the hours cases (minted fresh)
# Expected: 201
# @name hoursMgrSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Hours Manager",
  "email": "probe-hours-mgr-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234595"
}

### 21 — Setup: login the hours manager
# Expected: 200
# @name hoursMgrLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{hoursMgrSignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 22 — Create a store WITH operating hours (ticket 0011)
# Expected: 201 — response echoes openTime 09:00:00, closeTime 17:00:00 and
# the five working days
# @name createWithHours
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Clockwork Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{hoursMgrLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "12 Market Road, Lagos",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "clockwork-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  },
  "openTime": "09:00:00",
  "closeTime": "17:00:00",
  "workingDays": ["MONDAY", "TUESDAY", "WEDNESDAY", "THURSDAY", "FRIDAY"]
}

### 23 — Create with closeTime before openTime
# Expected: 400 — title "Invalid store hours". Hours are optional, but when
# both times arrive together, close must be after open
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Time Warp Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "KIOSK",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{hoursMgrLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "45 New Address, Ikeja",
    "phone": "08087654321",
    "email": "time-warp-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  },
  "openTime": "17:00:00",
  "closeTime": "09:00:00"
}
